_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Avoid leaving dead `PENDING` donations behind when Stripe session creation fails.**

The donation row is inserted before `checkout.sessions.create`. If Stripe throws, that row is never cleaned up and remains `PENDING` without a `stripeCheckoutSessionId`, so retries can accumulate unusable donations. Please either compensate on failure or only persist the row once the session is created.  


<details>
<summary>Possible localized fix</summary>

```diff
   const donation = await this.prisma.donation.create({
     data: {
       organizationId: campaign.organizationId,
       userId: input.userSub,
       campaignId: campaign.id,
       mode,
       cadence: input.cadence,
       amountCents: input.amountCents,
       currency,
       status: DonationStatus.PENDING,
       stripeCustomerId: customer.stripeCustomerId,
     },
   });

-  const session = await this.stripeClient.stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
-    ...
-  });
+  let session;
+  try {
+    session = await this.stripeClient.stripe.checkout.sessions.create({
+      ...
+    });
+  } catch (error) {
+    await this.prisma.donation
+      .delete({ where: { id: donation.id } })
+      .catch(() => undefined);
+    throw error;
+  }

   await this.prisma.donation.update({
     where: { id: donation.id },
     data: { stripeCheckoutSessionId: session.id },
   });
```
